17. In view of the above mentioned, the following:
ORDER a) The above appeal is partly allowed;
b) The judgment and award dated 15.12.2012 passed in M.V.C. No.751/2010 by the Court of Fast Track-III & Addl. M.A.C.T at Tumkur is modified to the extent ordered herein.

In all other aspects, the judgment and award of the Tribunal shall remain unaltered;
c) The appellant who is the 3rd respondent before the Tribunal is liable to pay a sum of Rs.50,000/-
together interest @ 6% per annum to the 1st respondent/claimant from the date of petition, till the date of payment;
d) The amount deposited by the appellant before this Court be transmitted to the Tribunal for disbursement in terms of the award;
Ramarao vs Channappa on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61722949/
5 - 11 - NC: 2024:KHC:2366 e) The appellant shall deposit the remaining amount together accrued interest within 8 weeks from the date of receipt of the copy of this judgment;
f) Consequent to deposit made, the amount shall be disbursed in terms of the award of the Tribunal.
Sd/-
JUDGE HKV Ramarao vs Channappa on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/61722949/
